ok - a dead session-end lane is relaunched once and then left alone
ok - an unchanged slot refusal is reported once and not retried by successor scanners; a changed cause permits one attempt
ok - an unchanged slot refusal is not retried after a new generation or an unrelated commit; a real change to the obstruction permits one attempt
ok - a long drift report keeps its durable reference through the fallback cap; a short one stays whole
ok - a failure that is not a refusal keeps today's retry
ok - each clone provisioner refusal text is a refusal: reported once by its line and not retried while unchanged
ok - the complete drift report reaches the observer on a relaunch and on a dirty refusal
ok - two printed reports are listed once, with a count that matches the paths, in the wake and in the durable file
ok - a sampled drift report carries its count and the file listing every path in the wake, through the length cap, and the durable file
ok - a real sampled report's sample line is true in the wake, where its first entry follows it
ok - a complete drift report whose path holds the sample marker is called complete on a relaunch and a refusal
ok - a could-not-be-produced report is kept as its one header line in the durable file
ok - the relaunch hands control the watcher's home, state, and a launch wait inside its bound
ok - a missing endpoint with session-end is not relaunched
ok - the relaunch bound stays at least 60s inside the watcher grace and refreshes the beacon first
ok - the 30-minute cap holds and wakes once
ok - the daily cap holds and wakes once
ok - deliberate exit, pause, hold, done, and a live agent are skipped
ok - an old /exit in the pane and an older exit marker do not suppress a later session-end relaunch
ok - one scan runs at most one relaunch and the next scan takes the next lane
ok - a lane whose captain hold cannot be read is not relaunched
ok - a backlog captain hold is not relaunched
ok - claude debug is off by default, on for a claude relaunch, and refused for another harness or a fresh spawn
